        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this file:\n\n- **Right unit**: The length check lives inside `normalizeTelephone`'s validation sequence, extracted into a well-named private helper `hasValidNationalNumberLength`. It sits alongside the existing length guard (`8..15`) as a natural next step, and the single call site reads clearly.\n- **Matches existing conventions**: This file already co-locates a documented static lookup `Map` with its consuming method (`ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` next to `normalizeAddress`). The new `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` map placed next to the telephone logic mirrors that pattern exactly, so a maintainer would find the placement natural rather than surprising \u2014 even though the field sits between methods.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all**: The `Owner` model already owns email/telephone/address normalization as the \"single source of truth\"; this addition fits that established responsibility without bloating anything or repeating existing code.\n- **Sound abstraction**: Using an ordered map keyed by country code with a longest-prefix-first comment, and treating unregistered codes as unconstrained, is an extensible, self-documenting design that will accommodate future country codes without structural change.\n\nThe Javadoc on both the method and the new helper/constant is consistent in tone and detail with the rest of the class."
